J1 MISS on all four pairs by the letter (NOSURVEY digests != NT): the model-written .py files differ from the NT baselines' (09: pricing/discounts.py; 10: utils/duration.py + tests/test_duration.py), passes equal (3/3 = 3/3), and NT's 10 runs failed their first pytest where J-NOSURVEY's passed first time. The main conversation's first request is byte-identical between NT and J-NOSURVEY (35B/09: system 9834 chars, same sha256; same user, same 25 tools, max_tokens 8192), so the build did not change the prompt: the difference is the pod's basin between ~01:00 and 03:25 UTC on identical input (rb-10827 class). J2-J5 are therefore scored within this chain only, as the rule requires.
J2 HOLDS: opening listing calls 0,0,0 under the survey vs 3,3,3 without, on every (model, task) — the prediction landed exactly.
J3 MISS on J-SURVEY-35B-10: 1/3 against NOSURVEY 3/3 — a survey cost on a task that was wide-basin without it; by the letter this heads the review (F9 class) and REOPENS the survey default. Mechanism (dumps, names only): without the survey the 35B lists the tree three times and reads pyproject.toml FIRST; with it, it reads slug.py first and pyproject.toml fourth; the two failing runs' verifier tail is ruff's docstring-section rule from [tool.ruff] ("Add blank line after Raises"). No run in any arm (J or NT, 24 + 12 runs) ran the project's lint (make lint / ruff); every shell call was pytest.
J4 MISS on (35B, 10): 16,17,17 vs 9,9,9. Holds on the other three; 27B/10 dropped from 15,15,15 to 11,11,8 — beyond the predicted 12-13.
J5: wall medians SURVEY <= NOSURVEY on 3 of 4 (38.0 vs 46.5; 38.4 vs 51.1; 209.3 vs 214.8); slower on 35B/10 (240.0 vs 185.5).
J6 HOLDS: 24/24 completed; harness_verify/project_verify 0 in every run (the model runs pytest itself; the rows carried trace_interventions as #427 intended).
Consequence by the letter: the survey default is reopened. The decisive instrument for an outcome question on a task the survey makes near-tie is basin sampling (ADR-0160, rb-10849) — arm K, pre-registered separately (survey-basin-10-preregistration.log); the durable fix the mechanism points at is a check the model cannot skip (review lever L4, Zak-Code #429, arm L).
